es>J-C</given-names></name><name><surname>de Murcia</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Poly(ADP-ribose): novel functions for an old molecule</article-title><source><italic>Nature Reviews Molecular Cell Biology</italic></source><year>2006</year><volume>7</volume><issue>7</issue><fpage>517</fpage><lpage>528</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16829982</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><label>6</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Beneke</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>B&#x000fc;rkle</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Poly(ADP-ribosyl)ation in mammalian ageing</article-title><source><italic>Nucleic Acids Research</italic></source><year>2007</year><volume>35</volume><issue>22</issue><fpage>7456</fpage><lpage>7465</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17913748</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><label>7</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hassa</surname><given-names>PO</given-names></name><name><surname>Hottiger</surname><given-names>MO</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The diverse biological roles of mammalian PARPS, a small but powerful family of poly-ADP-ribose polymerases</article-title><source><italic>Frontiers in Bioscience</italic></source><year>2008</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>3046</fpage><lpage>3082</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17981777</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><label>8</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>B&#x000fc;rkle</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Caselli</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Franceschi</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Pathophysiology of aging, longevity and age related diseases</article-title><source><italic>Immunity &#x0002